“In real-time, I use df -h to check overall filesystem usage and identify if any partition is full. Once identified, I use du -sh to drill down into directories and find what is consuming space, such as logs or backups. For memory, I use free -m to monitor RAM and swap usage. High swap usage usually indicates memory pressure, which can impact application performance. I typically combine these checks during troubleshooting when a system becomes slow or unresponssive"
